; LCNC-SUITE ORIGINAL — not vendored from upstream.
;
; Plane-mode "→ Zero": retract along the TOOL AXIS to a clearance, then X0 Y0
; in the plane. Called by the gateway's `go_to_zero` command when the Plane
; jog frame is active (kins 2, G59 — the plane fixture):
;
;     o<twp_goto_zero> call [clearance] [metric]
;
; #1 = clearance in MACHINE units (the gateway picks 25 mm / 1 in),
; #2 = 1 on a metric machine, 0 on an inch machine: G21/G20 is set
;      EXPLICITLY so #1 and the live position are read in the same units
;      whatever the caller had in force.
;
; Why a subroutine (TWP-01, review 2026-09-14): the gateway used to submit
; `G0 Z25` / `G0 X0 Y0` as bare MDI lines, inheriting the interpreter's
; distance mode and units — under G91 that is +25 of Z and no X/Y move at
; all; under G20 on a metric machine "25" is 25 inches. M73 saves the
; caller's modal state and restores it at endsub (G90/G91, G20/G21, …),
; the same shape as probe_basic/go_to_zero.ngc for the Machine frame.
;
; Order matters: the fixture guard comes BEFORE any modal change — an
; `(abort,…)` does not run M73's restore, so nothing may have changed when
; it fires. "Never lower" is decided HERE from the live plane Z (#<_z>, the
; current position in the active fixture including offsets), not from a
; status snapshot that may be a tick old; the M66 drains the queue first so
; that position is current (the same reliance twp_touchoff.ngc places on
; it). No rotary word anywhere: a rotary move would un-orient the head. An
; interpreter error during the Z leg aborts the sub before the X/Y leg.
o<twp_goto_zero>sub
(WEBUI_SUB=twp_goto_zero) ;lcnc-suite: preview sub-span marker, silent in task

o100 if [#5220 NE 6]
    (abort, twp_goto_zero: G59 - the plane fixture - is not active. Select the Plane frame again)
o100 endif

M73                                        ;save caller modal state, restore at endsub
G90                                        ;absolute distance mode
o110 if [#2 EQ 1]
    G21
o110 else
    G20
o110 endif
M66 L0 E0                                  ;force sync, stop read ahead: #<_z> is current
o120 if [#<_z> LT #1]
    G0 Z#1                                 ;retract along the tool axis — never lower
o120 endif
G0 X0 Y0                                   ;plane X0 Y0 (the datum, through G59)

(WEBUI_SUB_END) ;lcnc-suite: preview sub-span marker
o<twp_goto_zero>endsub
M2
